              "locator": "claim:P159:0",
              "original_text": "{\"property\": \"P159\", \"property_label\": \"headquarters location\", \"statement_id\": \"Q1054047$9AF22B38-566D-4873-B329-4F10205E8DE1\", \"rank\": \"normal\", \"snaktype\": \"value\", \"value\": {\"entity-type\": \"item\", \"numeric-id\": 37701, \"id\": \"Q37701\"}, \"qualifiers\": {\"P281\": [{\"snaktype\": \"value\", \"value\": \"9300\"}], \"P17\": [{\"snaktype\": \"value\", \"value\": {\"entity-type\": \"item\", \"numeric-id\": 258, \"id\": \"Q258\"}}], \"P625\": [{\"snaktype\": \"value\", \"value\": {\"latitude\": -29.12138889, \"longitude\": 26.21361111, \"altitude\": null, \"precision\": 0.00027777777777778, \"globe\": \"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q2\"}}]}}",
              "source_ref": "s1"
            }
          ],
          "id": "c1",
          "value": {
            "language": "en",
            "text": "The Central University of Technology, Free State (CUT) is a public university of technology in South Africa's Free State province. It operates campuses in Bloemfontein and Welkom, while Wikidata identifies Bloemfontein as its headquarters location. The institution traces its establishment to 1981, when it was known as Technikon Free State. During a later restructuring of South African tertiary education, it attained university of technology status; the available source does not provide an exact year for that change.\n\nCUT describes its teaching across technological fields alongside management sciences, humanities and education. Its four faculties cover Engineering, Built Environment and Information Technology; Health and Environmental Sciences; Humanities; and Management Sciences. The university lists undergraduate certificates and diplomas, advanced diplomas, postgraduate diplomas at honours level, and master's and doctoral degrees. The source also describes an academic and research workforce of more than 800 across these faculties.\n\nAn undated Wikipedia infobox reports 21,993 students and 1,100 administrative staff, while an undated Wikidata claim gives 1,500 employees; these figures have no shared reporting period and should not be treated as directly comparable. The infobox names Vincent Maphai as chancellor and Pamela Dube as vice-chancellor. CUT's published motto is “Thinking Beyond.”"
          },
          "verification": "supported"
        }
